**What's new this run:**
- **Level exit (G3c), previously never observed, now works.** A new probe, `exit_pickup.mjs`, walks to the real E1M1 exit switch and presses Use. The game shows the "HANGAR FINISHED" stats screen, then loads E1M2, where the player can move. All 8 checks pass. The intermission music and level music both started, health carried over, and there were no page errors. I looked at the screenshots, and they show the right screens in correct colours.
- **Item pickup works.** Walking onto a health bonus raised health from 100 to 101 and played the pickup sound. The intermission's items 2% agrees with that pickup.
- I used the noclip cheat to travel to the exit room, but turned clipping back on before the pickup and before pressing Use. So the exit itself ran normally, but the walking route to it was not tested.

**Same as the last review:**
- The build is byte-identical to the one the previous gameplay review tested (source hash 441e441a), so I didn't rebuild.
- All 8 earlier gameplay probes passed again: movement and momentum (stops 42 tics after release), pause and menu, focus loss and hidden-tab key release (10/10), cheats and weapons, and damage and death. Every sound effect requested was played (22 of 22), with no audio errors.

**My own probe mistakes, kept in the log folder as failing evidence:**
1. I used `IDCLIP`, which only works in Doom II. The shareware noclip cheat is `IDSPISPOPD`.
2. I stood 93 units from the switch, beyond Use's 64-unit reach.
3. I pressed Enter to leave the stats screen, but in the original game only Fire or Use advances it.

None of these was a fault in the port. One early version of the stats-screen check passed when it shouldn't have, and I fixed it before the passing run.

